Overall, all three countries saw a significant increase in internet access over the period. Japan had the highest figure throughout, while Viet Nam recorded the most dramatic growth.

In 2000, around a third of Japanese households (34%) were connected to the internet, compared with only 5% in Thailand and 2% in Viet Nam. The figure for Japan rose steadily to 71% in 2008 and then increased more slowly, reaching 93% in 2020.

Thailand and Viet Nam followed a similar pattern. The percentage of Thai households with internet climbed to 45% in 2012 and finally 80% in 2020. Meanwhile, Viet Nam started from the lowest point but grew rapidly, especially after 2008, and the figure reached 74% at the end of the period, only six percent lower than Thailand.', NULL, NULL, 151, DATEADD(minute,1210,CAST(DATEADD(day,-21,@today) AS datetime2(0))), 0, N'Published', 5.5, 5.5, NULL, 5.5, 5.0, NULL, 5.5, NULL, NULL, N'Bố cục rõ ràng, có overview/quan điểm cụ thể. Cần mở rộng ý bằng ví dụ cụ thể hơn và đa dạng từ nối thay vì Firstly/Secondly. Chú ý vài lỗi mạo từ.', NULL, NULL, DATEADD(minute,1230,CAST(DATEADD(day,-19,@today) AS datetime2(0))), DATEADD(minute,555,CAST(DATEADD(day,-18,@today) AS datetime2(0))));

