Overall, young people spend the most time on social media, while old people watch TV the most.

People aged 16-24 spend 18 hours on social media, which is the highest. They spend 7 hours watching TV, 6 hours for sport and only 2 hours reading. For the 25-44 group, social media is 11 hours and TV is 9 hours.

Older people is different. People from 45 to 64 watch TV 13 hours a week and the 65+ group watch TV 21 hours. They also read more, 5 and 8 hours. However, they spend very little time on social media and sport, only 2 hours for the oldest group.', NULL, NULL, 129, DATEADD(minute,1200,CAST(DATEADD(day,-5,@today) AS datetime2(0))), 0, N'Published', 6.0, 6.0, NULL, 6.0, 5.5, NULL, 6.0, NULL, NULL, N'Bố cục rõ ràng, có overview/quan điểm cụ thể. Cần mở rộng ý bằng ví dụ cụ thể hơn và đa dạng từ nối thay vì Firstly/Secondly. Chú ý vài lỗi mạo từ.', NULL, NULL, DATEADD(minute,1230,CAST(DATEADD(day,-3,@today) AS datetime2(0))), DATEADD(minute,555,CAST(DATEADD(day,-2,@today) AS datetime2(0))));

The most striking feature is the inverse relationship between age and the use of social media and television. As age increases, time spent on social media declines steadily, while television viewing rises markedly. Physical exercise, meanwhile, remains the least popular activity across the board.

Social media is by far the dominant pastime for 16-24-year-olds, who spend 18 hours a week on it, more than double the time they allocate to television (7 hours). This figure drops to 11 hours for the 25-44 group and falls to a mere 2 hours among those aged 65 and above.

Television follows the opposite trajectory, climbing from 7 hours for the youngest group to 21 hours for the oldest, making it the single most time-consuming activity in the entire chart. Reading shows a similar, though less dramatic, upward trend, increasing from 2 to 8 hours, whereas time devoted to sport gradually decreases from 6 hours to just 2.', NULL, NULL, 185, DATEADD(minute,990,CAST(DATEADD(day,-5,@today) AS datetime2(0))), 0, N'Draft', 7.0, 6.5, NULL, 6.5, 6.0, NULL, 6.5, NULL, NULL, N'Bài viết rất tốt: lập luận chặt chẽ, từ vựng học thuật phong phú, ít lỗi ngữ pháp. Có thể rút gọn một vài câu dài để tăng độ mạch lạc. Giữ phong độ nhé!', NULL, NULL, DATEADD(minute,1230,CAST(DATEADD(day,-3,@today) AS datetime2(0))), NULL);

Overall, social media was the most popular activity among younger people, whereas watching TV dominated the free time of older age groups. Time spent on sport was relatively low for all ages.

The 16-24 age group spent 18 hours a week on social media, far more than on any other activity. They watched TV for 7 hours and did sport for 6 hours, while reading accounted for only 2 hours. A similar pattern can be seen in the 25-44 group, although the gap between social media (11 hours) and TV (9 hours) was much smaller.

In contrast, people aged 45-64 and over 65 spent most of their leisure time watching TV, at 13 and 21 hours respectively. These two groups also read more than younger people, with the figure reaching 8 hours for the oldest group. However, social media use fell sharply with age, to just 2 hours a week among those over 65.', NULL, NULL, 178, DATEADD(minute,1335,CAST(DATEADD(day,-5,@today) AS datetime2(0))), 0, N'Submitted', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

